{"Allowing negative offsets with queryset[start_offset:stop] when enable_advanced_features=True triggers a COUNT(*) query which defeats the performance optimization purpose": 0.661172091960907, "Redirect depth limit was reduced from 10000 to 1000 without explanation, which could silently truncate segment merges for trace trees with depth >1000": 0.8839701414108276, "Redirect depth limit should have a comment explaining the rationale and expected depth bounds": 0.4065149426460266, "Redirect depth limit should be exposed as a configurable parameter via ARGV instead of hardcoding": 0.055956676602363586, "Redirect depth limit should have metrics to track when the limit is hit": 0.16768427193164825, "1000-span hard limit uses zpopmin which evicts based on end_timestamp_precise scores, so spans with identical timestamps will be evicted in lexicographic order by payload, not FIFO": 0.5073124766349792, "1000-span limit should be configurable via ARGV to allow operational tuning without code changes": 0.011081133037805557, "1000-span limit should emit a metric when eviction occurs to track frequency and inform capacity planning": 0.10829412192106247, "The max_segment_spans check was removed creating a silent behavioral change: previously segments exceeding max_segment_spans would be logged and skipped, now they're silently capped at 1000": 0.7068958878517151, "Need to verify max_segment_spans and the Lua limit are aligned, or add a comment explaining why the check is no longer needed": 0.2613297402858734, "Negative offsets could potentially access data beyond intended boundaries if the queryset isn't properly filtered, creating authorization bypass risk": 0.1360374242067337, "The authorization check for advanced features is unclear about what security boundary it protects and should be explicitly documented": 0.010483499616384506, "If advanced features enable broader data access via negative offsets, the queryset filtering should be audited to ensure it's sufficient": 0.042117804288864136, "No backward compatibility for legacy Redis Set keys during deployment; in-flight spans could be lost if not properly drained before rollout": 0.774156928062439, "Multiple spans with identical end_timestamp_precise values will be ordered lexicographically by payload, creating unpredictable eviction and pagination behavior that lacks test coverage": 0.29940155148506165, "Both 1000-span cap and 1000-depth redirect limit are embedded in Lua code, requiring full deployment to adjust, reducing operational flexibility": 0.025646567344665527, "Reduced redirect depth limit from 10000 to 1000 without observability metrics, risking silent behavioral changes and incomplete debugging": 0.4962075650691986}